<title>USA: Microelectronic names interim president.</title>
<headline>Microelectronic names interim president.</headline>
<dateline>SAN DIEGO 1996-11-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Microelectronic Packaging said it named Alfred Jay Moran, senior managing director of The Watley Group interim president and chief executive officer replacing Timothy da Silva, who resigned effective December 31 to join a unit of Xerox Corp in a senior management position.</p>
<p>The company also named Lewis Solomon and Anthony Bryan to the board, increasing the number of directors to five. Solomon was also named chairman of the MPI board.</p>
<p>Additionally, the company's board of directors has engaged The Watley Group , a consulting company, to advise it on strategic, management and financial restructuring matters.</p>
